 take over as interim athletic director at Texas A&M, effective Dec. 1, replacing the departed Trev Alberts.","published":"2026-11-23T22:07:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50576559/texas-names-john-thornton-interim-ad-effective-dec-1","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Giants DC Dennard Wilson interviews for HC job at alma mater Maryland","description":"Giants defensive coordinator Dennard Wilson had a virtual interview recently for the vacant head coaching job at Maryland, sources told NFL Network.","published":"2026-11-23T21:22:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50575838/sources-giants-dennard-wilson-interviews-maryland-job","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"LSU's Lane Kiffin apologizes for using profanity during halftime interview","description":"LSU coach Lane Kiffin has apologized for using profanity during a halftime interview with the school's radio network in Saturday's loss to Tennessee.","published":"2026-11-23T20:12:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575735/lsu-kiffin-apologizes-use-profanity-interview","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest leading rusher Ty Clark ruled out for season","description":"Wake Forest running back Ty Clark will miss the rest of the season, coach Jake Dickert announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-23T20:30:43.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575731/wake-forest-leading-rusher-ry-clark-ruled-season","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Syracuse rules QB Steve Angeli (shoulder) out vs. Notre Dame","description":"Syracuse has ruled starting quarterback Steve Angeli out for Saturday's game against Notre Dame due to a shoulder injury.","published":"2026-11-23T18:40:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575118/syracuse-rules-qb-steve-angeli-shoulder-vs-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana not yet naming starting QB for game vs. Purdue, Curt Cignetti says","description":"Indiana is not yet naming a starting quarterback for Saturday's rivalry game against Purdue, coach Curt Cignetti said Monday.","published":"2026-11-23T18:51:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575086/indiana-not-yet-naming-starting-qb-game-vs-purdue","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama's Kalen DeBoer expects QB Keelon Russell to be 'full go' vs. Auburn","description":"Alabama coach Kalen DeBoer said Monday that he expects QB Keelon Russell, who is working his way back from an ankle injury, to be \"full go\" for rivalry week against Auburn.","published":"2026-11-23T18:13:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50574915/alabama-deboer-expects-qb-russell-full-go-auburn","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5127738/ashton-hampton","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashton_Hampton"},"pick":{"pick":8,"round":1,"team":"NO","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Ashton Hampton","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashton_Hampton","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:22Z","intro":"Ashton Hampton (born January 9, 2006) is an American college football cornerback for the Clemson Tigers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Hampton attended Florida State University High School in Tallahassee, Florida, where he played cornerback and wide receiver. He was the All-Big Bend Defensive Player of the Year his senior year after recording 64 tackles and three interceptions. During his career he had 92 tackles and six interceptions on defense and 115 receptions for 1,797 yards and 21 touchdowns as a receiver. Hampton committed to Clemson University to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Hampton earned immediate playing time his freshman year at Clemson in 2024. He started four of 14 games and had 30 tackles and two interception, one that was returned for a touchdown. He started all 13 games his sophomore year in 2025, recording 45 tackles and one interception."}]}}